wlroots is the modular library that wayland compositors such as dwl are built on:
DRM/KMS output, libinput input, a scene graph and the common protocol implementations.
Built with the DRM and libinput backends and the software (pixman) renderer only: no
mesa/GLES2, Vulkan, gbm, Xwayland or color management yet, so no GPU acceleration and
no X11 apps. Installs libwlroots-0.20, headers and wlroots-0.20.pc under /usr/local.
The source is the Ubuntu archive's copy of the upstream release tarball (upstream's
own host is not reachable from the author's build box); the pin is of that file.
upstream: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/wlroots/wlroots
